Not that I haven't whimsically tried to persuade my fellow developers
that you should have to ascend before you can complete an Ubuntu
installation, but this isn't strictly true as stated; NetHack is not
actually present on Ubuntu CDs themselves. Anyone can download
precompiled binaries from the Ubuntu archive without going near
nethack.org or SourceForge or whatever, though. (Also most Ubuntu CDs
are downloaded for free or otherwise given away rather than sold; those
sound more like best-guess download numbers.)

Full Debian CD sets do include NetHack, although I don't think most
people bother with full Debian CD sets these days. Anyone can likewise
download precompiled binaries from the Debian archive.

